# Testing

Order: business logic → boundaries (auth/validation) → money-path or
other irreversible integration. Not framework internals, getters, or
styling.

Public surface only. Name states the behavior. Mock true externals
only. Flaky = broken (fix or declare-and-delete same day).

Bug fix ships a regression test named or described
`regression: <symptom>` that fails on old code.
Coverage is a smoke detector, not a trophy.

House gauntlet (Martin): confidence comes from constraints that already
exist — TOOLCHAIN, acceptance/Gherkin, unit tests, coverage or mutation
when the repo runs them — not from the human reading agent code. Do not
invent a mutation or Clean Architecture theater. ACT NOW — run what is
wired yourself; fail closed on red; cite evidence before Done. No house
gauntlet + land code → run closest real verify; name residual; never ask
accept-no-gauntlet-risk; no silent Done.
